<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fort Sumter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1861</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fort Sumter, on 12–13 April 1861, opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>, when Confederate batteries bombarded the federal fort in the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charleston-south-carolina">Charleston, South Carolina</a>. Its garrison under Major Robert Anderson surrendered after a day and a half. Lincoln's call for volunteers that followed led four more Southern states to secede.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fort-sumter.jpg" alt="Battle of Fort Sumter" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Currier &amp;amp; Ives. Uploaded by Christophe cagé 12:52, 6 September 2006 (UTC) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bombardment_of_Fort_Sumter.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
